<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5688" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Brĭăreus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trisyl.</span></b> ), ei,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βριαρεύς</span>, Callim.
		Del. 143 (old form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βριάρεως</span>, Hom. Il.
		1, 403; v. Crus. Wb. of Prop. Names), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the hundred-armed giant</i>, <i>also called Ægœon</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">centumgeminus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 6, 287</span></i>
			 Serv. and Heyne; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 10,
			565</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ferox,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					4, 596</span></i>
			 Schol.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">immensus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 2, 596</span></i>
			; cf. also <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 2, 10</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Claud. Laud. Stil. 1, 304</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vastus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Herc. Oet. 167</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Brĭă-rēĭus</span></b> ,
				a um, adj., <i>of</i> or
				<i>belonging to Briareus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Rapt. Pros. 3, 188</span></i>
			.</div>
